    "message": "fix(ingest): check containment against the file actually opened\n\nContainment was pure path arithmetic, which cannot see through a\nsymlinked directory: every segment of \"./linked/tsconfig.json\" is inside\nthe workspace even when `linked/` points elsewhere, so an ingested repo\ncould still choose a file outside the tree by shipping one link. The\nlexical check stays — it is what stops `../` traversal from the config\ntext — and the resolved path is now checked as well.\n\nThe resolve happens while the handle is open and is confirmed to name the\nsame inode, so swapping the link between the open and the resolve cannot\nsmuggle an outside file in under an inside name.\n\nThe workspace root is resolved too. Comparing a resolved file against an\nunresolved root rejects every config whenever the root is itself reached\nthrough a link — macOS /var -> /private/var, a home on a network mount, a\n~/code symlink — which would have switched tsconfig resolution off for\nthose users with no error. The matrix here is ubuntu + windows, so no\nrunner would have caught it; the added test uses a symlinked root.",
